const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'Which UAE port should I choose right now: Jebel Ali or Khalifa Port?',
    a: 'Choose by business model and final destination. Jebel Ali is the Middle East re-export and consumer-goods hub backed by JAFZA; Khalifa Port is the Abu Dhabi deep-water and KIZAD industrial option. Re-export/consumer flows lean Jebel Ali, while project cargo, heavy industry and Abu Dhabi-local delivery lean Khalifa.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is Khalifa Port a real alternative to Jebel Ali?',
    a: 'Yes. The port profile describes Khalifa Port as newer, deeper and generally less congested, and notes its KIZAD zone is attractive for importers doing assembly, storage or distribution in the UAE. For heavy or project cargo it often wins on draft and space.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Which port is deeper?',
    a: 'Khalifa Port, at ≈ 18 m versus Jebel Ali’s ≈ 17 m. The Khalifa profile describes it as among the deepest in the Gulf, which matters for project cargo and heavy industry.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Which port should I use for GCC re-export?',
    a: 'Jebel Ali. Its profile describes it as the region’s re-export engine: cargo often lands at Jebel Ali and is re-shipped onward to Saudi Arabia, Qatar, Kuwait and beyond, with JAFZA providing duty-deferred consolidation.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Which port is better for project cargo?',
    a: 'Khalifa Port. The profile says it is newer, deeper and less congested, and that for heavy or project cargo it often wins on draft and space. Confirm heavy-lift and laydown capacity with AD Ports Group before booking.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Who operates Jebel Ali and Khalifa Port?',
    a: 'Jebel Ali is operated by DP World, while Khalifa Port is operated by AD Ports Group. The Khalifa terminal is semi-automated and has expanded capacity toward 9m+ TEU.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is one port cheaper than the other?',
    a: 'The port profiles do not publish freight rates or terminal fees, so no price comparison is made here. The structural difference is congestion and onward-leg logic: Khalifa is the less congested capacity play, while Jebel Ali adds an onward feeder/truck leg for non-UAE destinations.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What should I confirm before choosing a UAE destination port?',
    a: 'Confirm the final consignee location, free zone versus mainland customs treatment, onward feeder or truck leg for non-UAE cargo, cut-offs and terminal congestion, and a live all-in quote. The port profiles do not publish rate or transit figures.',
